#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#Generic D-Class Sedan (Mid-Size) with Strut front and Tri-Link Strut rear suspension.
#
#D-Class vehicles include the Alfa Romeo 159, Audi A4, BMW 3 Series, Cadillac CTS, Lexus IS, and Mercedes-Benz C-Class.
#
#In this example, the engine (and any rigid parts which move together with the engine, e.g. transmission, clutch/torque converter) is treated as a single independent rigid body from the chassis (sprung mass).
#
#Details on engine body location and how the engine is mounted are specified on another screen: Engine Mounts: Engine Mass and Geometry. This is linked from the sprung mass dataset "D-Class, Sedan w/ Powertrain Mount.
#
#The engine body also reacts in the pitch / roll directions with the drive torque through the drive shafts and/or propeller shaft(s).
#
#The drive torque reactions are specified on the Powertrain screen (See the checkbox for "Front drive torque pitch effect").
#
#Updated for CarSim 2017:  Revised the steering system parameters.  Tested for: On-Center, Static Steer, and Free Response Stability.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: Vehicle: Assembly; { D-Class } D-Class, Sedan 2017 (PT Mounts, FF Based AWD)
